cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use distillops, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "distillops: black-box LLM distillation for any verifiable task"
abstract: >-
  distillops distils an API language model into a small open model for any task with a
  verifiable answer: it collects teacher answers, keeps those that pass the task's verifier
  (rejection sampling), fine-tunes the student (SFT), evaluates it, and runs reinforcement
  learning (GRPO) with the task's score as reward. Only the teacher's text answers are needed,
  never its logits.
authors:
  - family-names: Wu
    given-names: Zihao
repository-code: "https://github.com/Zihao-Wu06/distillops"
url: "https://github.com/Zihao-Wu06/distillops"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
keywords:
  - knowledge distillation
  - large language models
  - rejection sampling
  - supervised fine-tuning
  - reinforcement learning
  - GRPO
  - small language models
